From 988ed8fdb63c558ff27e7fcaf86765c4cac2ee19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tudorek12345 <44846825+tudorek12345@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:20:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Recover sparse texture pages and retain remap invalidations

Adapt focused discovery and notification fixes from DexNom/VIctory 921d8d3b43b44f3a6ca4b44095edd3c4baf10a87. Preserve the mapped-view fast path; inspect interior memory regions when endpoint pages are absent, exclude guard and inaccessible regions, and reject overflowed ranges. Collapse a full bounded notification queue into a rescan of registered texture spans instead of dropping changes. The interior-page regression fails on f09 mapped_bytes (0 versus 65536) and passes after this fix; six focused CPU regressions pass. No runtime FPS or RAM improvement is claimed.
